# Linken engineering rules

## Language
- Product UI and copy: English only.

## File size (hard)
- Prefer ≤120 lines per file.
- Soft max 150. Never exceed 200 lines in one file.
- If approaching the limit: split by responsibility (UI / data / actions / types).
- Route files (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`) stay thin — compose only.

## Architecture
- App Router routes are shells. Logic lives in `src/components`, `src/features`, `src/lib`.
- One concern per file. No god components.
- Shared primitives in `src/components/ui`.
- Domain UI in `src/components/{company,partners,layout}`.
- Types in `src/types`. Mock data in `src/data/mock` until backend is connected.
- No backend/Supabase wiring until the correct account is linked.

## Scalability & cost
- Prefer Server Components. Mark `"use client"` only when needed.
- No heavy UI kits, animation libraries, or chart libs unless explicitly requested.
- Avoid client-side data fetching for static/mock pages.
- Keep dependencies minimal. Optimize for Vercel free/hobby until scale requires more.

## Egress (critical)
- Never burn egress without a clear product need.
- No polling, no speculative prefetch storms, no downloading large assets "just in case".
- Prefer local mock data and Server Components until the correct backend is connected.
- Do not call external APIs, Supabase, or remote storage unless explicitly required for the task.
- Images: local/static first; never hotlink large remote media in loops.
- When backend exists: fetch only required fields, cache where safe, avoid N+1 client waterfalls.

## Design
- Enterprise B2B: calm, precise, trustworthy. Not playful SaaS kitsch.
- Follow tokens in `globals.css`. Do not invent one-off colors in components.
- Partners live in a right-hand rail on company profiles.
